  W/R is the setting being soaked right now and steps is how many times this
  bank has had to slow down to get there. A bank with no errors yet is bounded,
  not proven, and the bound falls as this runs. One that errors steps slower and
  starts its count again, so the settings converge on what survives sustained
  load rather than on what looked fine while the board was still cold.
